# .dockerignore
# --------------
# Keeps the build context small and hermetic for BOTH Dockerfiles in this repo
# (ml/Dockerfile and Dockerfile.backend), which share the repository root as
# their context. Without this the daemon receives the whole repo, including the
# ~3 GB venv/, the uploads/ corpus and .git/ -- gigabytes neither image needs
# nor should see.
#
# The ML service needs: detector.py, the model weights, ml/, and the Phase 1
# golden fixture used by the parity check.
# The backend needs: the Flask modules, templates/ and static/.
#
# Both are ~equal, so a single root .dockerignore is the right shape; a second
# one would require moving sources into a subdirectory.

.venv/
venv/
env/
ENV/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/

.git/
.gitignore
.github/
.opencode/
skills/

# Runtime state and test artifacts -- never part of an image
uploads/
letters/
*.db
*.db-journal
*.log
.env
.env.*

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Flask application (Phase 5)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Phase 3/4 excluded these because the Flask app was not yet containerized, and
# `Dockerfile.backend` cannot COPY a file the context does not contain.
#
# They are now INCLUDED in the context so the backend image can be built. This
# does NOT put them into the ML image: ml/Dockerfile COPYs only the files it
# explicitly names (detector.py, models/, ml/, the golden fixture), so these
# extra context entries are simply transferred and then discarded. The cost is
# ~70 KB.
#
# `tests/` remains NOT excluded as a directory. Docker's .dockerignore cannot
# re-include a file whose parent directory is excluded, so excluding `tests/`
# would also drop the golden fixture ml/parity_check.py needs. Only the
# throwaway Python artifacts are dropped instead.
tests/__pycache__/
# models/ stays in the context for the ML image; Dockerfile.backend never
# COPYs it, so the 89 MB of weights never reach the backend image.

# Documentation and container plumbing
*.md
Dockerfile
docker-compose*.yml
